Description: Fix ToValueList to use std::move for projection results
 The ToValueList function uses std::ranges::for_each with a projection.
 When the projection returns a value type (like base::Value::Dict),
 std::ranges::for_each passes the result by reference to the callback.
 .
 The original code used std::forward<T>(value), but since the projection
 result is stored as an lvalue by for_each before passing to the callback,
 T deduces to a non-reference type and forward returns an lvalue reference.
 .
 This causes compilation errors because Value::List::Append(DictValue&&)
 requires an rvalue reference but receives an lvalue.
 .
 Fix by using std::move(value) unconditionally since the projection result
 is always consumed exactly once and should be moved into the list.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-03

diff --git a/base/containers/to_value_list.h b/base/containers/to_value_list.h
index 643ccd0..01735ae 100644
--- a/base/containers/to_value_list.h
+++ b/base/containers/to_value_list.h
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ Value::List ToValueList(Range&& range, Proj proj = {}) {
   auto container = Value::List::with_capacity(std::ranges::size(range));
   std::ranges::for_each(
       std::forward<Range>(range),
-      [&]<typename T>(T&& value) { container.Append(std::forward<T>(value)); },
+      [&]<typename T>(T&& value) { container.Append(std::move(value)); },
       std::move(proj));
   return container;
 }
